            <ArticleTitle>Causalgia: clarifications in terminology and a case presentation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>284-95</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>By way of literature review, clarifications are made in the terminology employed in discussing the atypical post-traumatic pain syndromes, particularly reflex sympathetic dystrophy (RSD). Causalgia is a form of RSD and is the focus of a case report presented from the files at St. Anne's Hospital-West, Northlake, Illinois.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
